  "bodyText": "Models Pricing Verification Docs Change language Toggle theme Sign in Get your key The model you pay for. From a verified provider. Sterling sends every request to a provider Mira Network has tested, so the model you pay for is the one that answers. See provider scores Get your key Three steps. Then the verified model. Create your key, get credits, and route through a verified provider. STEP 01 Create your key One key for Claude, GPT, Gemini and more. STEP 02 Add credit USDC or MIRA. Pay as you go. STEP 03 Get your model, verified Sterling checks the provider before it serves your request, so the model you pay for is the one you get. Routed only to providers that are verified. A model name on an API is a claim. Mira Network tests every provider behind Sterling on a schedule and publishes the result per model-provider pair, with the request and response behind each verdict. See Verification scores Model identity The provider's outputs are compared with a reference snapshot of the model it says it serves, across repeated runs. Tool calls Tools trigger when they should, with valid arguments, as often as the reference does. Parameters honoured The temperature, max_tokens and other parameters you send are the ones the provider applies. Silent failures No empty, truncated or malformed responses returned as if they were fine. Declared context The provider honours the context window it advertises. Shown as \"not yet tested\" until the check is switched on. Three steps. Then you're in. 01 Create your key. One key for every model on Sterling. 02 Add credit. Top up in USDC or MIRA, then pay as you go. 03 Plug into your app. Change the base URL. Keep your code. Change the endpoint. Keep your workflow. curl Copy code curl https://sterling.mira.network/v1/chat/completions \\ -H \"Authorization: Bearer $STERLING_API_KEY\" \\ -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\ -d '{ \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello\"}] }